# The Controller page with a virtual Xbox pad: its south button given Quick
# Save from the list, its north found by pressing it and given Quick Load,
# its right trigger found by pulling it and given the scope. The wizard
# opened by the pad's own south button, which it must not take for the
# first step: west pressed for it, the rest skipped. Then a controller SDL
# has no mapping for, its left trigger resting at the top, mapped by the
# wizard -- the face buttons, the trigger, the d-pad's up twice and its
# down, the rest skipped -- and Play: test_ui_scripts.c reads User.ini,
# gamecontrollerdb.txt and what the engine got.
pad attach xbox
wait 1.5
expect home
find Settings
key Return
wait 0.5
expect settings
find Controller
key Return
wait 0.5
find A
key Return
wait 0.3
expect pick
find Quick Save
key Return
wait 0.3
expect settings
find Find a button
key Return
wait 0.3
pad button 3 down
wait 0.15
pad button 3 up
wait 0.3
key Return
wait 0.3
expect pick
find Quick Load
key Return
wait 0.3
expect settings
find Find a button
key Return
wait 0.3
pad axis 5 1
wait 0.3
key Return
wait 0.3
expect pick
find Toggle scope
key Return
wait 0.3
pad axis 5 -1
wait 0.3

# The wizard by the pad's confirm, held as it opens.
find Layout
find Map this controller...
pad button 0 down
wait 0.3
expect padwizard
pad button 0 up
wait 0.8
pad button 2 down
wait 0.15
pad button 2 up
wait 0.3
find Skip
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
wait 0.3
expect settings

# A second controller, SDL's none: chosen above the model, mapped from the
# rows' end.
pad attach raw
pad axis 2 1
wait 0.5
find Controller
key Right
wait 0.3
find Layout
find Map this controller...
key Return
wait 0.3
expect padwizard
# Its trigger first read before it was at the top: the wizard takes where
# it rests once it has been still a second.
wait 1.5
pad button 0 down
wait 0.15
pad button 0 up
wait 0.3
pad button 1 down
wait 0.15
pad button 1 up
wait 0.3
pad button 2 down
wait 0.15
pad button 2 up
wait 0.3
pad button 3 down
wait 0.15
pad button 3 up
wait 0.3
find Skip
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
pad axis 2 -1
wait 0.2
pad axis 2 1
wait 0.3
find Skip
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
pad hat 0 1
wait 0.15
pad hat 0 0
wait 0.3
pad hat 0 1
wait 0.15
pad hat 0 0
wait 0.3
pad hat 0 4
wait 0.15
pad hat 0 0
wait 0.3
find Skip
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
key Return
wait 0.15
wait 0.3
expect settings
find Done
key Return
wait 0.5
expect home
find Play
key Return
wait 2.5
expect recovery
find Quit
key Return
